### Simple Tier (main only)

| Branch | Environment | Protection | Purpose |
|--------|-------------|------------|---------|
| `main` | Production | None | All development + releases |

```
main branch → commit directly → production
```

**When to use Simple:**
- Solo developer
- Small projects without release isolation
- Prototypes, spikes, personal projects
- Private repos with no external visibility needed

#### Daily Development

```bash
# Work directly on main
git checkout main
git pull origin main

# Make changes, commit directly
git add .
git commit -m "[type]: [description]"
git push origin main
```

#### Multi-Agent Development (Git Worktrees)

Use worktrees **only** when multiple agents need to work in parallel:

```bash
# Create worktree for parallel work
git worktree add ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--agent-2 main

# Work in the worktree
cd ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--agent-2

# When done, remove worktree
git worktree remove ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--agent-2
```

**Note**: All worktrees share `main`. Coordinate commits to avoid conflicts.

