### Standard Tier (main + dev)

| Branch | Environment | Protection | Purpose |
|--------|-------------|------------|---------|
| `main` | Production | Protected | Releases only (accepts PRs from dev) |
| `dev` | Staging | Unprotected | Active development (commit directly) |

```
dev branch → commit directly → staging
     ↓  (PR only)
main branch → production releases
```

**When to use Standard:**
- Public repos with production code on main
- Need release isolation without PR overhead
- Small teams (1-3 people) with fast iteration
- AI-assisted development workflows

#### Branch Protection Rules

**⛔ main branch** - ONLY accepts PRs from `dev`:
- Enforced by `.github/workflows/enforce-main-pr-source.yml`
- Any direct push or PR from other branches → REJECTED

**✅ dev branch** - Unprotected:
- Commit directly, no PR required
- Use worktrees for parallel agent work

#### Daily Development

```bash
# Ensure you're on dev
git checkout dev
git pull origin dev

# Make changes, commit directly
git add .
git commit -m "[type]: [description]"
git push origin dev
```

#### Multi-Agent Development (Git Worktrees)

Use worktrees **only** when multiple agents need to work in parallel on `dev`:

```bash
# Create worktree for parallel work
git worktree add ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--agent-2 dev

# Work in the worktree
cd ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--agent-2

# When done, remove worktree
git worktree remove ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--agent-2
```

**Note**: All worktrees share `dev`. Coordinate commits to avoid conflicts.

#### Releasing to Production

```bash
gh pr create --base main --head dev --title "Release v[version]"
# main ONLY accepts PRs from dev
```

