### Enterprise Tier (main + dev + feature branches)

| Branch | Environment | Protection | Purpose |
|--------|-------------|------------|---------|
| `main` | Production | Protected | Releases only (PRs from dev) |
| `dev` | Staging | Protected | Integration (PRs from feature/*) |
| `feature/*` | Local | N/A | Feature development |
| `fix/*` | Local | N/A | Bug fixes |

```
feature/fix branches → (PR) → dev → (PR) → main
```

**When to use Enterprise:**
- Large teams with multiple parallel features
- Multiple agents working on different features simultaneously
- External team collaboration requiring review
- Long-running stable projects past experimentation

#### Branch Protection Rules

**⛔ main branch** - ONLY accepts PRs from `dev`
**⛔ dev branch** - ONLY accepts PRs from feature/fix branches

#### Development Flow with Worktrees

Use worktrees to isolate parallel feature work:

```bash
# Create worktree for feature (from main repo on dev)
git worktree add ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--feature-auth -b feature/auth origin/dev

# Work in the worktree
cd ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--feature-auth

# Create PR to dev
git push -u origin feature/auth
gh pr create --base dev --head feature/auth

# After PR merged, remove worktree
git worktree remove ../{{PROJECT_NAME}}--feature-auth
```

#### Worktree Directory Convention

```
~/repos/
├── {{PROJECT_NAME}}/                    # Main repo (stays on dev)
├── {{PROJECT_NAME}}--feature-auth/      # Feature worktree
├── {{PROJECT_NAME}}--feature-payments/  # Another feature
└── {{PROJECT_NAME}}--fix-oauth/         # Bug fix worktree
```

#### Releasing to Production

```bash
gh pr create --base main --head dev --title "Release v[version]"
```

